# dtlab_config.local.env.example — template for a PERSONAL, MACHINE-LOCAL
# override of dtlab_config.env.
#
# This fork's tracked dtlab_config.env already defaults to OpenAI
# (DTLAB_PROVIDER='openai', gpt-5-nano / gpt-5-mini). Use this local
# override file for your OWN sandbox when you want something different
# on just your machine without touching the tracked config — e.g.
# falling back to Anthropic, or trying a different OpenAI model.
#
# To use it:
#   1. Copy this file to ~/dtlab/dtlab_config.local.env
#        cp provisioning/dtlab_config.local.env.example \
#           ~/dtlab/dtlab_config.local.env
#      (student_start.sh sources it, if present, right after
#      dtlab_config.env — so it overrides just these settings.)
#   2. Uncomment/edit the block you want below.
#
# NEVER commit the real dtlab_config.local.env file — it is (and must
# stay) covered by .gitignore. This .example file is the only copy
# that belongs in git.

# ---- Option A: fall back to Anthropic on this machine only ----
# DTLAB_PROVIDER='anthropic'
# DTLAB_MODEL_ECONOMY='claude-haiku-4-5-20251001'
# DTLAB_MODEL_FRONTIER='claude-sonnet-5'

# ---- Option B: stay on OpenAI but pin different model IDs ----
# DTLAB_PROVIDER='openai'
# DTLAB_MODEL_ECONOMY='gpt-5-nano'
# DTLAB_MODEL_FRONTIER='gpt-5-mini'
